ArrayList is the class name and Add is a method in these contracts. The contracts include Add(), Remove(), Insert(), Set(), Get(), and Contains(). These contracts are using PexFramework and written using C#.

In general, for each method, we are making assumptions (we are saying that the preconditions that we are testing must be true), and then observing after the call whether or not the postconditions (what the method is supposed to do) are still valid. The PexObserve.ValueForViewing() is used to log values for observation and debugging purposes.

Note: The above information is for adding contracts to the ArrayList class using the PexFramework. The specifics may differ for your actual ArrayList class. But the overall concept and methodology should remain the same.

