The PexFramework is actually an automated property-based testing framework designed to increase confidence in your code because it finds a large number of potential edge and corner cases, but is more than capable of generating a small, manageable number of testcases. For some more complex classes, it can generate hundreds of test cases and catch some pretty nasty corner cases early on. But you run into a problem where it can take forever (or never terminate/run out of time) if your test cases aren't right.
